  "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $Y$ is a function $F(y)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(y)=P(Y\\le y).\n$$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(2) & =P(Y\\le 2) \\\\  & =P(Y\\in {0,1,2}) \\\\  & =P(Y=0)+P(Y=1)+P(Y=2) \\\\  & =f(0)+f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & =0.10+0.05+0.45 \\\\  & =0.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
